.SH NAME
niac-scenario-apply - Validate and display scenario information


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac scenario apply  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Validate a scenario and display its configuration details.
This command loads the scenario, validates it, and shows what devices
and protocols it contains without creating a file.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for apply


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Validate basic network scenario
  niac scenario apply basic-network

  # Check data center scenario
  niac scenario apply data-center

  # Verify IoT network configuration
  niac scenario apply iot-network
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBniac-scenario(1)\fP


